                <head>No. 705.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram from secretary of state, Madrid, to
                        Spanish minister, Washington. Received November 28, 1873, 9.15
                    a.m.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">[<date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content-and-sibling-dates"
                            calendar="gregorian" notAfter="1873-11-28" notBefore="1873-11-12"
                            >undated</date>].</dateline></opener>
                <p>Negotiations renewed in Madrid. Confer again with Mr. Fish on the basis of the
                    last official note, [official telegram ?] and renew to him the assurances of the
                    good faith and rectitude of our proposition; assuring him likewise that our
                    agreement, whatever it may be, shall be beyond all doubt carried out in
                    Cuba.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
